<h3>
100% IV Mr. Rime
</h3>

<p>

A 15/15/15 Mr. Rime is commonly called a Hundo or
100% IV Mr. Rime. It is particularly desirable for
collectors and for formats where maximum IVs are useful.

</p>


<div class="best-move">

<strong>
100% Mr. Rime Checklist
</strong>

<p>
15 Attack + 15 Defense + 15 Stamina = 100% IV
</p>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     PVP
========================================================= -->

<section class="section" id="pvp">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
Mr. Rime PvP Guide
</h2>

<p>

Mr. Rime can use moves such as Icy Wind and Psychic
for charged-move pressure, although it is not generally
considered a top-tier PvP Pokémon.

</p>

</div>


<h3>
Great League
</h3>

<p>

Great League requires careful IV selection because
Mr. Rime must remain below the league's CP limit.
A low-Attack, higher-Defense/HP spread can sometimes
be preferred for CP-limited formats.

</p>


<h3>
Ultra League
</h3>

<p>

Ultra League gives Mr. Rime more room to reach a higher
level, but its overall ranking remains dependent on the
current metagame, moves and available opponents.

</p>


<h3>
Master League
</h3>

<p>

Mr. Rime can reach 3,196 CP at Level 50, but its
Master League performance is generally more limited
than that of the format's strongest meta Pokémon.

</p>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     EVOLUTION
========================================================= -->

<section class="section" id="evolution">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
Mr. Rime Evolution
</h2>

<p>

Mr. Rime evolves from Galarian Mr. Mime. It is not
an evolution of the standard Kantonian Mr. Mime.

</p>

