</div>

<h3>
XXL Mr. Rime
</h3>

<p>

An XXL Mr. Rime can be useful for collection,
Pokédex size records and activities where Pokémon
size matters.

</p>

</div>


<h3>
XXL Does Not Mean 100% IV</h3>

<p>

A common mistake is assuming that a very large Pokémon
must have excellent IVs. Size and IVs are separate
characteristics. An XXL Mr. Rime can have low, average
or perfect IVs.

</p>


<ul class="checklist">

<li>
XXL is a size characteristic.
</li>

<li>
XXL does not automatically mean Hundo.
</li>

<li>
XXL can coexist with Shiny status.
</li>

<li>
XXL can coexist with Lucky status.
</li>

<li>
XXL can be part of a collector's size collection.
</li>

</ul>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     XXS
========================================================= -->

<section class="section" id="xxs">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
XXS Mr. Rime
</h2>

<p>

XXS Mr. Rime is the opposite size category from XXL.
Its size does not determine its IVs or battle statistics.

</p>

</div>


<div class="variant-card size-card">

<span class="special-badge badge-perfect">
📐 XXS
</span>

<div class="variant-icon">
📐
</div>

<h3>
XXS Mr. Rime
</h3>

<p>

An XXS Mr. Rime can be kept as a collection specimen,
especially by trainers interested in size records.

</p>

</div>


<h3>
XXS and IVs</h3>

<p>

XXS status and IV quality are separate characteristics.
An XXS Mr. Rime can have any IV combination, including
0/0/0 or 15/15/15.

</p>

</section>


