<!-- =========================================================
     CANDY
========================================================= -->

<section class="section" id="resources">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
Mr. Rime Candy, XL Candy & Stardust
</h2>

<p>

Building a high-level Mr. Rime requires Candy,
Candy XL and Stardust. Because Mr. Rime is not
normally a first-choice raid attacker, consider
your intended use before making a large investment.

</p>

</div>


<ul class="checklist">

<li>
Keep strong-IV Mr. Rime specimens for long-term projects.
</li>

<li>
Save Candy XL for Pokémon you actually intend to power up.
</li>

<li>
Check the moveset before spending Elite resources.
</li>

<li>
Compare Mr. Rime with other Ice and Psychic attackers.
</li>

<li>
Lucky Mr. Rime can be attractive for Stardust-efficient investment.
</li>

</ul>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     AVAILABILITY
========================================================= -->

<section class="section" id="availability">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
Mr. Rime Availability
</h2>

</div>


<p>

Mr. Rime availability can depend on Pokémon GO's
current events, evolution requirements and encounter
rotations. Because availability can change, avoid
hard-coding an old event date as a permanent method
of obtaining Mr. Rime.

</p>


<div class="best-move">

<strong>
Current Availability
</strong>

<p>
Check the current Pokémon GO event and encounter
schedule before planning a Mr. Rime hunt.
</p>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     BATTLE GUIDE
========================================================= -->

<section class="section" id="battle-guide">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
How to Use Mr. Rime
</h2>

</div>


<h3>
For PvE
</h3>

<ul class="checklist">

<li>
Choose an Ice moveset when Ice damage is required.
</li>

<li>
Choose a Psychic moveset for Psychic-type coverage.
</li>

<li>
Check the current raid meta before investing heavily.
</li>

<li>
Compare Mr. Rime with stronger alternatives.
</li>

</ul>


<h3>
For PvP
</h3>

<p>

Icy Wind can provide useful attack-debuff utility,
while Psychic gives Mr. Rime another charged-move
option. Shield management and IV selection are
important in CP-limited leagues.

</p>


<h3>
For Collectors
</h3>

<p>

Mr. Rime becomes considerably more interesting as a
collection target when combined with Shiny, Shadow,
Lucky, Hundo, XXL and XXS characteristics.

</p>

</section>


