<!-- =========================================================
     FAQ
========================================================= -->

<section class="section" id="faq">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
Mr. Rime FAQ
</h2>

</div>


<details>

<summary>
What type is Mr. Rime?
</summary>

<p>
Mr. Rime is an Ice/Psychic-type Pokémon.
</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
What is Mr. Rime weak to?
</summary>

<p>

Mr. Rime is weak to Bug, Dark, Fire, Ghost,
Rock and Steel attacks.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
What does Mr. Rime evolve from?
</summary>

<p>

Mr. Rime evolves from Galarian Mr. Mime.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
What is Mr. Rime's max CP?
</summary>

<p>

Mr. Rime reaches 3,196 CP at Level 50 with
perfect IVs.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Is Shiny Mr. Rime available?
</summary>

<p>

Yes. Shiny Mr. Rime is available in Pokémon GO.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Is Shadow Mr. Rime available?
</summary>

<p>

Shadow Mr. Rime is available as a Shadow variant.
Availability can depend on the current Team GO
Rocket rotation.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Can Shadow Mr. Rime be purified?
</summary>

<p>

An eligible Shadow Mr. Rime can be purified.
Purification removes the Shadow status and changes
the Pokémon's characteristics.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
What is a 100% Mr. Rime?
</summary>

<p>

A 100% or Hundo Mr. Rime has 15 Attack,
15 Defense and 15 Stamina IVs.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
What is a Lucky Mr. Rime?
</summary>

<p>

Lucky Mr. Rime is obtained through trading.
Lucky Pokémon have special trade-related
characteristics, including reduced Stardust
requirements for powering up.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Can Mr. Rime be XXL?
</summary>

<p>

Yes. XXL is a size characteristic and is separate
from IV quality.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Can Mr. Rime be XXS?
</summary>

<p>

Yes. XXS is a size characteristic and does not
determine IV quality.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Can Shiny Mr. Rime also be Lucky?
</summary>

<p>

Yes. Shiny and Lucky are separate characteristics,
so a traded Shiny Mr. Rime can have Lucky status.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Can a Shadow Mr. Rime be Shiny?
</summary>

<p>

Shiny Shadow availability depends on the current
Pokémon GO Shadow encounter pool and events.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Is Mr. Rime good for raids?
</summary>

<p>

Mr. Rime can provide Ice or Psychic damage, but its
overall raid value should be compared with stronger
specialized attackers before making a major investment.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Is Mr. Rime good in PvP?
</summary>

<p>

Mr. Rime can use useful charged attacks such as
Icy Wind and Psychic, but its PvP value depends on
the league, moveset and current metagame.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
What is the best Ice moveset for Mr. Rime?
</summary>

<p>

Ice Shard and Triple Axel are a strong Ice-focused
combination to consider, subject to current move
availability.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
What is the best Psychic moveset for Mr. Rime?
</summary>

<p>

Confusion and Psychic provide a Psychic-focused
moveset option.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Does XXL Mr. Rime mean 100% IV?
</summary>

<p>

No. Size and IVs are separate characteristics.
An XXL Mr. Rime can have any IV combination.

</p>

</details>


<details>

<summary>
Does XXS Mr. Rime mean bad IVs?
</summary>

<p>

No. XXS status does not determine IV quality.
An XXS Mr. Rime can even be a 15/15/15 Hundo.

</p>

</details>

</section>


